  "assets": "assets/scenes/entryway_eva_slippers",
  "implementation_policy": "Two EVA slides on a stone entryway floor: compressible volumetric FEM (StableNeoHookean with a native objective-viscosity extension, runtime/native/pcve_viscosity) and two-way IPC contact in libuipc (CUDA, bdf2), production tetrahedral geometry accepted_delivery/geometry_d, sampled at exactly 24 Hz for 4 s; the optional wooden shoe tray is a finite-mass affine body. tools/native/simulate.py (source, stiff_falling, remove_resting, add_shoe_tray with vocab_hero.py) and simulate_revision.py (slippery_floor, light_falling with vocab_revised.py) solve one case; render_hero.py replays the exact FEM surface vertices in Blender; tools/native/realism.py is the look of the published videos. tools/launch.py starts both through tools/native/pool_worker.py (GPU preflight, lease, UUID binding). --stage verify checks the accepted native delivery (strict edits, videos and native caches against each case's artifact manifest and render binding, 24 Hz clocks). Materials are effective values, not calibrated.",
